                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "What if Total War was made on a budget of three buttons and pure napoleonic spite? You spend two real-time hours manually marching 500 French infantrymen across an open field in perfect formation, only for the entire regiment to get permanently stuck inside a wooden barn while a single Austrian cannon sniper obliterates your general from three miles away. The naval battles are just wooden ships slowly turning into each other like hyper-aggressive drift cars, and the campaign map UI looks like an old Excel spreadsheet that hates you. You start the game aiming for total European enlightenment, but within 20 minutes you're screaming at line-infantry ragdolls who are refusing to reload because a fence is in their way. 10/10 strategic bayonet dumpster fire.",
